{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"artifactsRead\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/test-plan.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/quick-fix/002-quick-fix.json\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/boundary.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Follow-up verification focused on F-06-001, the trailing-turnless newest-closed-turn shape, directly touched boundary decision code, directly touched tests, production-path audit terms, focused tests, story gate, and epic gate.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[{\"id\":\"F-06-001\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"rationale\":\"Resolved by code and test evidence. `advanceDecision` now stops before the last candidate with a non-null `turnId`, protecting the newest closed turn and any later turnless singleton. The added TC-5.2 test covers two closed turns followed by a trailing turnless singleton and asserts boundary remains before the newest closed turn. The prior production-path probe now passes with `boundary: 3`, `zoneTokens: 130`, and rows t1/order 3, t2/order 7, trailing null/order 10.\"}],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"F-06-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Trailing-turnless protection creates an unresolved AC-5.3 landing-window exception\",\"evidence\":\"AC-5.3 still says the advance lands in `[target, target + one turn)`. The new trailing-turnless TC-5.2 leg in `view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` uses budgets 100/60 with groups t1=50, newest closed t2=45, trailing turnless=70, then expects boundary after t1 and `zoneTokens` 115. If the next protected turn is the newest closed turn, the AC window is `[60, 105)`, so the expected 115 is outside it. This is not a code failure in the quick fix; it exposes a product/spec ruling needed for the legal trailing-turnless shape because a scalar boundary cannot both skip the trailing singleton and preserve the newest closed turn. The story technical notes were changed to protect trailing turnless singletons after the newest closed turn, but the AC wording and tech-design.md Flow 5 still carry the general landing-window phrasing.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.3\",\"TC-5.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"F-06-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Trailing-turnless protection creates an unresolved AC-5.3 landing-window exception\",\"evidence\":\"AC-5.3 still says the advance lands in `[target, target + one turn)`. The new trailing-turnless TC-5.2 leg in `view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` uses budgets 100/60 with groups t1=50, newest closed t2=45, trailing turnless=70, then expects boundary after t1 and `zoneTokens` 115. If the next protected turn is the newest closed turn, the AC window is `[60, 105)`, so the expected 115 is outside it. This is not a code failure in the quick fix; it exposes a product/spec ruling needed for the legal trailing-turnless shape because a scalar boundary cannot both skip the trailing singleton and preserve the newest closed turn. The story technical notes were changed to protect trailing turnless singletons after the newest closed turn, but the AC wording and tech-design.md Flow 5 still carry the general landing-window phrasing.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.3\",\"TC-5.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"F-06-001: newest closed turn remains intact when a trailing turnless singleton follows it; verified by added test and production-path probe.\",\"AC-5.1/TC-5.1: focused suite remains green for turn-end-only advance and mid-turn stability.\",\"AC-5.2: focused suite remains green for whole-turn eviction and singleton turnless behavior in covered cases.\",\"AC-5.4: focused suite remains green for two-field config defaults and max > target validation.\",\"AC-5.5/TC-5.3: focused suite remains green for forward-only behavior, deterministic replay, compact reset, and post-commit failure healing in the amended tests.\",\"Configured story gate: `pnpm run verify` passed.\",\"Epic gate: `pnpm run verify-all` passed.\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-5.3 landing interval for legal trailing-turnless-after-newest-closed-turn zones needs a human ruling or explicit spec exception before handoff.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"cd packages/lhc && pnpm exec tsx -e '<AC-5.3 trailing-turnless newest-closed production-path probe>'\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"cd packages/lhc && pnpm exec vitest run test/view-boundary.test.ts test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapter, shim, placeholder branch, hidden floorTokens fallback, or non-real boundary advance surface was found in the reviewed production files.\",\"The prior production-path bug is fixed, but the trailing-turnless shape now exposes an unresolved AC-5.3 landing-window scope question.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"needs-human-ruling\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"openQuestions\":[\"For a legal zone with a newest closed turn followed by one or more turnless singleton groups, is the `[target, target + one turn)` landing guarantee allowed to have an exception so the newest closed turn remains protected?\"],\"additionalObservations\":[\"The focused suite count increased from 19 to 20 tests; full suite count increased from 376 to 377 passed tests, with 9 env-gated skips.\",\"`tech-design.md` still states the older Flow 5 shorthand of excluding the newest group always, while the touched story notes now describe stopping before the newest closed turn and protecting trailing turnless singletons.\"]}"}}
